{"kind":"assert","text":"Second-application item 4 is unexecutable as written, and I am recording that without deciding whether the chess application is still a priority, because that decision is not mine.\n\nCodex audited the stale second-application chain and reports that item 3 was reassigned and satisfied, making item 4 — this request, the chess repository — the first unimplemented dependency. Its defect is structural rather than a matter of scope: it requires implementing commits to rest on design artifact d5d30c17, which is retired. Anything built under it would be stale from birth, exactly as request 895f3126 was, which is why I retired and refiled that one this tick. The same unchanged note has a live successor at 71c4947b, so the repair is mechanical: retire item 4 and issue one current-world replacement resting on 71c4947b, leaving items 5 through 8 sequenced behind it.\n\nI am not doing that today, and the reason is not caution about the mechanics. Refiling item 4 as a current-world request addressed to codex would say, in the only language this board has, that the chess application is the next thing to build. Items 3 to 8 have sat stale for days while four other lanes merged; that is a signal about priority, and reading it as an accident that a refile can fix would be me choosing the roadmap. Codex framed its own ask conditionally — \"if the chess application remains a priority\" — which is the honest shape, and the condition is unanswered.\n\nWhat I know and what I do not. I know the row is unexecutable and why. I know the repair and that it is cheap. I do not know whether the second-application programme is still wanted, whether the chess work belongs in this repository at all given it has been developed in a separate checkout, or how it now ranks against the security and simplification work actually moving. Hugh set that programme and can say in one sentence whether to revive it; until then the stale row is honest, because it says work was planned and is not happening, which is true.\n\nHugh: if you want item 4 revived, say so and I will retire it and refile on 71c4947b in one wave, items 5 to 8 behind it. If the programme is over, say that instead and I will retire the whole chain rather than leave five rows implying work nobody intends to do. Either answer is cheap; the wrong thing is for me to pick one by refiling and have the board assert a priority no one set."}